{"lines": ["In Taos, New Mexico, in the early 1990s, residents complained of a low, droning hum that most of their neighbors could not hear.", "A study found at least two percent of people could hear it, each at a different pitch somewhere between thirty-two and eighty hertz.", "Middle-aged people were more likely to hear it. Men and women heard it in about equal numbers.", "Hums like it have been reported in Australia, Canada, Britain, and the United States.", "In Windsor, Ontario, one evening in 2012 brought twenty-two thousand reports to officials.", "The sound seemed to come from Zug Island, a steel-mill district across the Detroit River.", "When the blast furnaces there shut down in April 2020, the noise went away too.", "But that's one hum solved. Researchers say the Hum is not a single phenomenon.", "Industrial machines explain some. Tinnitus and the way the ear works explain others. The Taos Hum has never been pinned to one source.", "For some people, a sound nobody else can hear is the most frightening signal of all.", "Still, a hum is only a sound. The next signal had a face."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.14], ["Taos,", 0.14, 0.64], ["New", 0.88, 1.04], ["Mexico,", 1.04, 1.42], ["in", 2.0, 2.08], ["the", 2.08, 2.18], ["early", 2.18, 2.44], ["1990s,", 2.44, 4.06], ["residents", 4.3, 4.74], ["complained", 4.74, 5.3], ["of", 5.3, 5.68], ["a", 5.68, 5.74], ["low,", 5.74, 5.96], ["droning", 6.68, 7.0], ["hum", 7.0, 7.22], ["that", 7.22, 7.58], ["most", 7.58, 7.82], ["of", 7.82, 8.04], ["their", 8.04, 8.16], ["neighbors", 8.16, 8.52], ["could", 8.52, 8.8], ["not", 8.8, 9.0], ["hear.", 9.0, 9.28], ["A", 9.86, 9.92], ["study", 9.92, 10.14], ["found", 10.14, 10.48], ["at", 10.48, 10.7], ["least", 10.7, 10.8], ["two", 10.8, 11.06], ["percent", 11.06, 11.42], ["of", 11.42, 11.58], ["people", 11.58, 11.82], ["could", 11.82, 12.12], ["hear", 12.12, 12.34], ["it,", 12.34, 12.52], ["each", 12.96, 13.14], ["at", 13.14, 13.38], ["a", 13.38, 13.5], ["different", 13.5, 13.72], 